# A screenshot the system takes shows up by itself in the list that hovering the Library button
# opens, next to the downloads, as Arc's Library button had it (byearc's "Screenshots in Library").
# Spotlight finds it by macOS's screen-capture mark, so Library ▸ Media's Show Media (off here, as in
# a new data folder) doesn't hold it back, and no folder is read to list it. The picture goes in the
# real ~/Pictures (Spotlight doesn't index a throwaway home) and is deleted at the end.
budget rss=600 stalls50=5
cra://debug?fakeScreenshot=Cra%20scenario%20screenshot.png
expect-log fake screenshot: Cra scenario screenshot.png
# Spotlight's live update can take half a minute: ask once a second for up to a minute.
pace 1
repeat 60 cra://debug?downloadsList=shown
pace 0.2
expect-log downloads list shown: .*screenshot:Cra scenario screenshot.png
cra://debug?downloads=1
wait 1
cra://debug?downloadsTray=open
expect-log downloads tray open: open=true
cra://debug?downloads=0
cra://debug?fakeScreenshot=-Cra%20scenario%20screenshot.png
wait 1
cra://debug?downloadsList=deleted
reject-log downloads list deleted: .*screenshot:Cra scenario screenshot.png
